export abstract anchor FactoryEvidence:
    artifactStore:
        Artifacts live outside the specification in a project-configured store
        with encryption at rest and an explicit reader authorization model.
        The store issues immutable identifiers. Artifacts are copied on attach,
        never referenced by mutable worktree or external URI. Every artifact
        records a content hash and an ingestion policy version. Conformance
        reports are write-once and may be appended only by an independent
        verifier principal; reader and writer roles are separate.
    requiredEvidence:
        Required evidence includes attempt records and summaries, the commit or
        a durable diff bundle with a pinned ref, build and test reports, review
        verdicts, delivery receipts, and the completion manifest. Harness logs
        and transcripts are captured when the harness supports retrieval;
        otherwise the attempt carries the available summary and a missing
        evidence marker. A pinned ref is protected from deletion or force
        update, or replaced by the durable diff bundle.
    ingestion:
        Writes follow write, hash verify, then commit reference. A failed write
        is retried or spooled; assessment sees evidence-pending rather than
        silently passing. Hashes are verified before assessment and recovery. A
        store outage is a blocker, not a completion.
        Ingestion scans for secrets and quarantines suspect content. Externally
        authored logs and diffs may still contain secrets. Quarantine has a
        release or denial workflow with an approver, a false-positive path, and
        an evidence waiver rule. Redaction happens before commit and records its
        policy version, a marker, and the original hash. A missed secret triggers
        a rescan, an incident, and credential rotation. Security deletion uses
        crypto-shredding or an equivalent tamper-evident path.
        Reader roles are engineer, scoped agent, and auditor.
    retention:
        Completed evidence manifests are retained indefinitely as metadata with
        hashes. Large artifacts default to 90 days, configurable with an
        engineer-approved floor and legal or security holds. Active and blocked
        orders retain artifacts indefinitely. Failed orders retain until a
        successor supersedes them or the engineer authorizes a retention
        release. A retention release is requested as an engineer question and
        authorized by its answer; it records an event with actor, scope, reason,
        and time, bumps the order version, and does not change the terminal
        state. Submitted orders are nonterminal and retain until they become
        active or cancelled; there is no separate resolution event. Deferred
        follow-up work pins its source evidence until it terminates.
        Retention clocks start at completion, cancellation, supersession, or
        retention release, in UTC. Hold authority and floor changes belong to
        the engineer.
    garbageCollection:
        Garbage collection uses transactional reference counting with a grace
        epoch. It never deletes a referenced artifact. An artifact written
        before its reference commits is protected by an orphan TTL defaulting to
        24 hours. Deletion uses mark, tombstone, delete, then outcome records,
        with retry. Expired artifacts leave tombstones with identifiers and
        hashes. Successor orders cite tombstones when content is gone.
        Quota exhaustion never evicts live evidence.
    manifest:
        The completion manifest has a canonical schema, is itself an immutable
        artifact, is hashed with SHA-256, and is frozen at completion. Audit
        entries carry artifact identifiers only when evidence must be retained;
        otherwise they carry hashes and metadata so retention can terminate.
        Status reports store outages, evidence-pending states, quota, and the
        age of the last successful write.
